    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d685">

                <pb facs="0698" n="594" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg594"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 815.77/76.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of the Navy to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of the Navy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-01-29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 29, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith, for
                    the information of the Department of State, a copy of a cablegram, dated January
                    27, 1912, from the Commanding Officer, U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Petrel</hi>,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d685-f1"/> in which it is stated that
                    there are well founded rumors that the Honduran Government, upon assuming
                    control February 1st, intends to take charge of railroad now leased to American
                    Company, and that it is deemed advisable for the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Petrel</hi> to remain at Puerto Cortés, Honduras.</p>
                <p>I have the honor, further, to state that instructions, by cable, were issued on
                    January 28th to the Commanding Officer, U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Petrel</hi>, to remain at Puerto Cortés at his discretion.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">George von L. Meyer</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
